In .NET MAUI, use the **lifecycle events** API in your `MauiProgram.cs` (or app builder configuration):

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is paused
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is stopped
        }));
#elif IOS
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // runs when the app enters background
        }));
#endif
});
```

You'll need:
```csharp
using Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents;
```

This maps directly to the native `OnPause`/`OnStop` (Android `Activity`) and `DidEnterBackground` (iOS `UIApplicationDelegate`) callbacks without requiring custom platform code or renderers.
